File Name: HandKinematics.py

Necessary Packages: numpy, scipy

Necessary Modules (files): None

Overview: This file interprets our filtered sensor data and stores the live details of the hand's current position. All
data sent to and received from this file must pass through GloveMonitorWindow.py. This data is used both for animation
and hand-position identification.

Methods: All methods are kept under the RightHand and Finger classes

----------------------------------- Finger Methods --------------------------------------------------------
__init__ (Finger): Called from within the RightHand class to generate finger objects. finger may be used to store and
access segment joint angles and segment lengths, as well as the finger's relative orientation to the wrist.

set_j1_flex: sets the flex measured on the middle finger joint

set_j2_flex: sets the flex measured on the front-most finger joint

get_j1_flex: gets the flex measured on the middle finger joint

get_j2_flex: gets the flex measured on the front-most finger joint

zero_orientation, set_orientation: POTENTIALLY USED to set finger relative orientation. Due to our quaternion implementation, this function
is not utilized.

get_orientation: POTENTIALLY USED to get finger relative orientation. Due to our quaternion implementation, this function
is not utilized.

------------------------------------ RightHand Methods ----------------------------------------------
__init__ (RightHand): sets thumb and finger segment lengths to be stored. This is unrelated to those stored in our
animation window. Additionally, creates thumb and finger objects for the hand. Initializes a dummy value for the
sampling rate which is dynamically updated later (In other words, the initial value is not significant). Creates variables
to store euler (presently unused) and quaternion values related to wrist gyro, then fingers gyro. Finally, initializes
correction matrices for gyro sensors (see gyro_calibration folder). These values are meant to correct the predictable
hardware-born errors due to our sensors and their actual installation.

update_sample_rate: sets new sample rate based on dynamically calculated value

set_j1_angles: sets angles of middle finger joints (across all 4 fingers and thumb) to be stored in our
created finger objects

set_j2_angles: sets angles of end finger joints (across all 4 fingers, NOT thumb) to be stored in our
created finger objects

get_j1_angles, get_j2_angles: retrieves joint angles from fingers and pushes them forward as our returned value

update_orientation: Calculates and updates angle of wrist gyroscope sensor based on our transformation matrices
(use as model for finger gyroscope transformations, THOUGH: THESE ARE BETTER DONE LINEARLY (without matrix B)).
Additionally, these values are stored as a usable 4-length vector (x, y, z, w)

update_orientation_fingers: similar to wrist, updates relative orientation on all fingers. Additional transformation of
backwards-calculating from finger tips to wrist utilizing other joint angles (again, not presently used (instead,
calculated later) as this required unreliable Euler angles)

zero_orientation: Zeros all stored data associated with glove live position

get_orientation: returns stored wrist gyroscope euler angle values (unused)

get_orientation_q: returns stored wrist gyroscope quaternion values (used)

get_relative_orientations: returns stored finger gyroscope euler angle values (unused)

get_relative_orientations_q: returns stored finger gyroscope quaternion angle values (used)

relative_q: computes relative quaternion angle of one finger compared to the wrist and returns it
(Utilized internally within get_relative_orientations_q).

get_j0_angles: returns angles for base segments for fingers (Unused, only relevant for Euler implementation)

j0_x: returns base joint angle of a finger based on euler implementation (internal to get_j0_angles, never accessed)


